error[ffi_macro_name]: `own.h` defines `v2467` as a macro that takes more arguments than the 1 this declaration gives it, and every call of it this program's C writes goes through the macro, which has no parameter types for clang to hold this declaration to
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2467-a-variadic-behind-a-macro-of-one-more-argument-is-told-as-the-macro.case/main.hero:10:5
     |
  10 |     function v2467(a: i32) -> i32  #~ ffi_macro_name
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: bind a function of the program's own that calls it: in a header beside this file, `static inline <C result> hero_v2467(<its parameters, in C>) { return v2467(<their names>); }`, with the C types the macro's documentation gives where the placeholders stand; then name that header in an `extern` group and declare `hero_v2467` there like any function, and clang holds that declaration to your function (§ 13)
